quand Matthieu dit « range / réorganise / renomme / déplace cette archive », « mets l'archive sous tel dossier », « trie l'archive comme sur mon Mac », ou archive un dossier DJI. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/skills/archive-organize/SKILL.md)\n- browser:control-in-app-browser: Control the in-app Browser for opening, navigating, inspecting visible or interactive page state, clicking, typing, screenshots, and local web testing. It can have existing signed-in sessions. For semantic operations on linked resources, prefer a purpose-built connector, API, or CLI when available. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-bundled/browser/26.707.51957/skills/control-in-app-browser/SKILL.md)\n- documents:documents: Create, edit, redline, and comment on `.docx`, Word, and Google Docs-targeted document artifacts inside the container, with a strict render-and-verify workflow. Use `render_docx.py` to generate page PNGs (and optional PDF) for visual QA, then iterate until layout is flawless before delivering the final document. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime/documents/26.709.11516/skills/documents/SKILL.md)\n- first-movement: Turn an intimidating creative or technical ambition into one visible, reversible first action. Use when the user invokes /first-movement, says they are stuck, overwhelmed, procrastinating, or unsure where to start, or wants to make a first animation, prototype, artwork, scene, tool, or any unfamiliar thing with AI. Especially use for Houdini, APEX, Unreal Engine, game development, art, learning, and other creative work where the real obstacle is initiating the first movement. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/skills/first-movement/SKILL.md)\n- gmail:gmail: Manage Gmail inbox triage, mailbox search, thread summaries, action extraction, reply drafting, and email forwarding through connected Gmail data. Use when the user wants to inspect a mailbox or thread, search email with Gmail query syntax, summarize messages, extract decisions and follow-ups, prepare replies or forwarded messages, or organize messages with explicit confirmation before send, archive, delete, or label actions. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/gmail/0.1.5/skills/gmail/SKILL.md)\n- gmail:gmail-inbox-triage: Triage a Gmail inbox into actionable buckets such as urgent, needs reply soon, waiting, and FYI using connected Gmail data. Use when the user asks to triage the inbox, rank what needs attention, find what still needs a reply, or separate important mail from noise. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/gmail/0.1.5/skills/gmail-inbox-triage/SKILL.md)\n- google-calendar:google-calendar: Manage scheduling and conflicts in connected Google Calendar data. Use when the user wants to inspect calendars, compare availability, review conflicts, find a meeting room, review event notes or attachments, add or adjust reminders, place temporary holds, or draft exact create, update, reschedule, or cancel changes with timezone-aware details. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/google-calendar/1.2.4/skills/google-calendar/SKILL.md)\n- google-calendar:google-calendar-daily-brief: Build polished one-day Google Calendar briefs. Use when the user asks for today, tomorrow, or a specific date summary with an agenda, conflict flags, free windows, remaining-meeting readouts, or a calendar brief, and the Google Calendar connector is available. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/google-calendar/1.2.4/skills/google-calendar-daily-brief/SKILL.md)\n- google-calendar:google-calendar-free-up-time: Find ways to open up meaningful free time in a connected Google Calendar. Use when the user wants to clear up their day, make room for focus time, create a longer uninterrupted block, or see the smallest set of calendar changes that would give time back. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/google-calendar/1.2.4/skills/google-calendar-free-up-time/SKILL.md)\n- google-calendar:google-calendar-group-scheduler: Find and rank good meeting times for multiple people using connected Google Calendar data. Use when the user wants to schedule a group meeting, compare candidate slots across several attendees, find the best compromise time, or add a room check after narrowing the attendee-compatible options. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/google-calendar/1.2.4/skills/google-calendar-group-scheduler/SKILL.md)\n- google-calendar:google-calendar-meeting-prep: Build a practical meeting prep brief from a connected Google Calendar event and its nearby context. Use when the user wants to prepare for an upcoming meeting, understand what to read beforehand, pull in linked notes or docs, or get a concise brief on what the meeting appears to require. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/google-calendar/1.2.4/skills/google-calendar-meeting-prep/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-docs: Connector-first Google Docs creation and editing in local Codex plugin sessions, with direct native create and batchUpdate workflows for simple docs, DOCX-first import for polished deliverables, target-document checks, smart chip and building-block reconstruction, connector-readback verification, and reference routing for formatting, citations, tables, and write-safety. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/google-drive/0.1.8/skills/google-docs/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-drive: Use connected Google Drive as the single entrypoint for Drive, Docs, Sheets, and Slides work. Use when the user wants to find, fetch, organize, share, export, copy, or delete Drive files, or summarize and edit Google Docs, Google Sheets, and Google Slides through one unified Google Drive plugin. (file: /Users/zenray/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/google-drive/0.1.8/skills/google-drive/SKILL.md)\n- google-drive:google-drive-comments: Write, reply to, and