ppshots  L679:   * cite250† Chrome extension  L680:   * cite251† Work with files  L681: \nL682: ### Reference\nL683: \nL684:   * cite252† Commands  L685:   * cite253† Slash commands  L686:   * cite254† Settings  L687:   * cite255† Troubleshooting  L688: \nL689: Copy Page\nL690: # Settings\nL691: \nL692: Configure preferences in the ChatGPT desktop app\nL693: \nL694: Copy Page\nL695: \nL696: Use the settings panel to personalize the app and manage everyday preferences. Open cite385†Settings†settings from the app menu or press\nL697: \nL698: `Cmd`+`,` on macOS or `Ctrl`+`,` on Windows.\nL699: ## General\nL700: \nL701: Require `Cmd`+`Enter` for multiline prompts, or turn on Prevent sleep while running so local tasks can continue while you step away. Under Follow-up behavior, choose whether a message sent while ChatGPT works should steer the current run or wait for the next run.\nL702: ## Profile\nL703: \nL704: Use Profile to review activity insights, lifetime tokens, peak tokens, streaks, your longest task, and token activity. You can also update your profile details, such as your picture, display name, and username, and save a profile card with usage highlights. Sharing profile cards is available on consumer ChatGPT plans.\nL705: Eligible users can also send Codex invitations from the profile menu. Choose Invite a friend on an eligible personal plan or Invite a coworker in an eligible Business workspace. See cite386†Invite friends and coworkers for current rewards, limits, and eligibility.\nL706: ## Keyboard shortcuts\nL707: \nL708: Open Keyboard Shortcuts to review commands, change bindings, or reset custom shortcuts to their defaults. Use the search field to find shortcuts by command name, or switch to keystroke search and press a key combination to find the command that uses it.\nL709: \nL710: ## Notifications\nL711: \nL712: Choose when turn completion notifications appear, and whether the app should prompt for notification permissions.\nL713: ## Appearance\nL714: \nL715: In Settings, you can change the app appearance by choosing a base theme, adjusting accent, background, and foreground colors, and changing the UI and code fonts. You can also share your custom theme with friends.\nL716: \nL717: cite389†Image: ChatGPT desktop app Appearance settings showing theme selection, color controls, and font options cite390†Image: ChatGPT desktop app Appearance settings showing theme selection, color controls, and font options L718: cite391†Image: ChatGPT desktop app Appearance settings showing theme selection, color controls, and font options cite392†Image: ChatGPT desktop app Appearance settings showing theme selection, color controls, and font options L719: ## Pets\nL720: \nL721: Pets are optional animated companions for the app. In Settings > Pets, choose a built-in or custom pet, then use `/pet`, Wake Pet, or Tuck Away Pet to control the floating overlay.\nL722: \nL723: See cite387†Pets to understand pet status, follow activity across tasks, or create your own pet.\nL724: \nL725: 1/8\nL726: \nL727: Codey I found a tiny loose thread in settings. Want me to tug it?\nL728: ## Browser\nL729: \nL730: Use these settings to install or enable the bundled Browser plugin, set up the cite250†Chrome extension , and manage allowed and blocked websites. ChatGPT asks before using a website unless you’ve allowed it. Removing a blocked site lets ChatGPT ask again before using it in the browser.\nL731: \nL732: See cite388†Built-in browser for browser preview, comment, and Computer Use workflows.\nL733: ## Computer Use\nL734: \nL735: Check your Computer Use settings to review desktop-app access and related preferences after setup. On macOS, revoke system-level access by updating Screen Recording or Accessibility permissions in macOS Privacy & Security settings.\nL736: ## Personalization\nL737: \nL738: Choose Friendly, Pragmatic, or None as your default personality. Use None to disable personality instructions. You can update this at any time.\nL739: \nL740: You can also add your own custom instructions. Editing custom instructions updates your cite264†personal instructions in AGENTS.md .\nL741: \nL742: ## Suggested prompts\nL743: \nL744: Use context-aware suggestions to surface follow-ups and tasks you may want to resume when you start or return to ChatGPT.\nL745: ## Memories\nL746: \n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019f55b4-f9b9-7661-9192-f516710a0f7b"}}}
